      "content": "hey i keep getting a CrashLoopBackOff on this microservice in our GKE cluster. i'm looking at the logs and it's not super clear. can u give me a diagnostic checklist to figure out if this is a resource limit issue, a liveness/readiness probe failure, or just a bad config? \n\nhere is the snippet of the logs:\n[error] container main-service exited with code 1\n[info] back-off restarting failed container\n[error] failed to create pod sandbox: rpc error: code = Unknown desc = failed to create containerd task: failed to create shim task: OCI runtime error: container_linux.go:380: starting container process caused: exec: \"start-app.sh\": executable file not found in $PATH",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
